The page only covers basic installation and vanilla usage. It doesn't include the React wrapper, CSS import, theme, resize, realtime API, performance, timeMultiplier, or tooltip/legend settings, so I can't extract those from it.

**What the page does cover:**

Install with `npm i @gravity-ui/yagr`, then create a chart from an element with a `timeline` and a `series` array. Each series has `data` and `color`:

```typescript
import Yagr from '@gravity-ui/yagr';

new Yagr(document.body, {
    timeline: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
    series: [
        {
            data: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
            color: 'red',
        },
        {
            data: [2, 3, 1, 4, 5],
            color: 'green',
        },
    ],
});
```

It also documents a script-tag version that loads `https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/yagr/dist/yagr.iife.min.js`.

**Where to find the missing details:**

- Versioned docs for this release: `https://gravity-ui.com/llms/yagr/5.3.1/llms.txt`
- Latest 5.x docs: `https://gravity-ui.com/llms/yagr/5/llms.txt`
- Full README: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gravity-ui/yagr/main/README.md`
- Changelog: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gravity-ui/yagr/main/CHANGELOG.md`
- Examples: the `demo/examples` folder in the GitHub repository

Check the `@gravity-ui/yagr` version in the project's `package.json` first. If it isn't 5.3.1, use the URL for that major version so the API details match.

